00:10:34,427 --> 00:10:35,757
That was the hard part. But once I was in,

256
00:10:35,797 --> 00:10:38,066
I had better blood circulation than the time I did...

257
00:10:38,067 --> 00:10:39,467
the lower body bath with hot water.

258
00:10:40,397 --> 00:10:42,867
(Thanks to the cold plunge, his immune cells are on fire.)

259
00:10:44,967 --> 00:10:46,767
(His immune system is strengthening.)

260
00:10:48,107 --> 00:10:50,607
(In no time, the bathroom is filled with some healthy energy.)

261
00:10:50,737 --> 00:10:51,777
My gosh.

262
00:10:52,607 --> 00:10:54,647
Come on, faster. Just ten more seconds.

263
00:10:55,577 --> 00:10:57,817
(His immune cells are making their last sprint for energy.)

264
00:10:58,617 --> 00:11:00,186
His hairy body will get so cold.

265
00:11:00,187 --> 00:11:01,257
(Time, move faster.)

266
00:11:02,217 --> 00:11:03,857
I guess your body won't get used to the cold.

267
00:11:03,917 --> 00:11:05,556
- The time moved so slowly. - It is moving slowly.

268
00:11:05,557 --> 00:11:06,986
You need determination for this.

269
00:11:06,987 --> 00:11:08,057
(It feels as if time had stopped during the last 10 seconds.)

270
00:11:08,327 --> 00:11:09,327
Stop.

271
00:11:09,328 --> 00:11:10,357
Thirty seconds.

272
00:11:10,457 --> 00:11:12,697
Gosh, it's so cold.

273
00:11:13,297 --> 00:11:15,296
(He gets up as soon as...)

274
00:11:15,297 --> 00:11:17,267
(his 2 minutes and 30 seconds are up.)

275
00:11:17,707 --> 00:11:18,767
It's so cold.

276
00:11:19,637 --> 00:11:22,477
It's so cold.

277
00:11:23,437 --> 00:11:24,706
- But didn't it feel refreshing? - Right.

278
00:11:24,707 --> 00:11:25,746
- It felt so refreshing. - Right.

279
00:11:25,747 --> 00:11:26,747
- It woke you up, right? - That's great.

280
00:11:26,748 --> 00:11:28,177
I felt blood circulating all over my body.

281
00:11:28,247 --> 00:11:30,076
It's so cold.

282
00:11:30,077 --> 00:11:32,017
(It was painful during the plunge, but it feels good afterward.)

283
00:11:32,917 --> 00:11:34,086
(Grabbing)

284
00:11:34,087 --> 00:11:35,157
It's so cold.

285
00:11:36,817 --> 00:11:37,927
Gosh, it's cold.

286
00:11:37,987 --> 00:11:39,027
This feels warm.

287
00:11:39,727 --> 00:11:40,757
Gosh, it's warm.

288
00:11:41,597 --> 00:11:42,927
- Yes, indeed. - My gosh.

289
00:11:43,027 --> 00:11:44,196
- His eyes are full of life. - Look at his eyes.

290
00:11:44,197 --> 00:11:45,327
- The swelling went down too. - Look at him.

291
00:11:45,767 --> 00:11:48,296
I definitely felt my body changing.

292
00:11:48,297 --> 00:11:50,297
It was like getting a brand-new body.

293
00:11:50,497 --> 00:11:52,006
Let's say you don't feel good.

294
00:11:52,007 --> 00:11:53,436
Doing a cold plunge makes your body feel brand-new.

295
00:11:53,437 --> 00:11:54,606
- Right. - You know what I mean, right?

296
00:11:54,607 --> 00:11:55,706
- It's... - You know since you're frail.

297
00:11:55,707 --> 00:11:57,106
If I feel healthy even for a bit, that feels weird to me.

298
00:11:57,107 --> 00:11:58,406
We think about how it'd be nice...

299
00:11:58,407 --> 00:12:00,806
- to get our body fixed, right? - Poison is all over our body.

300
00:12:00,807 --> 00:12:02,316
The bottoms of my feet are flat.

301
00:12:02,317 --> 00:12:04,077
And there are always knots in my calves.

302
00:12:04,217 --> 00:12:06,287
My calves always hurt even when I got massages.

303
00:12:06,447 --> 00:12:07,656
I did that for 2 minutes and 30 seconds.

304
00:12:07,657 --> 00:12:09,316
- And my calves felt so relaxed. - People say...

305
00:12:09,317 --> 00:12:10,616
- toxins build up in calves. - Really?

306
00:12:10,617 --> 00:12:12,356
- Massages take two hours. - Trying it once is worth it.

307
00:12:12,357 --> 00:12:13,456
- It's worth it. - Yes, it is. Try it.

308
00:12:13,457 --> 00:12:14,457
I strongly recommend it.

309
00:12:14,458 --> 00:12:17,496
I think cold plunges will be a trend.

310
00:12:17,497 --> 00:12:20,066
Jennie and Son Heung Min may have begun...

311
00:12:20,067 --> 00:12:21,366
the trend globally.

312
00:12:21,367 --> 00:12:23,067
But in Korea,

313
00:12:23,397 --> 00:12:25,437
I will lead the trend.

314
00:12:25,937 --> 00:12:28,506
The three of us have become the trend setters...

315
00:12:28,507 --> 00:12:29,807
for cold plunges.

316
00:12:31,077 --> 00:12:34,007
(The trend setter gets dressed after the cold plunge.)

317
00:12:34,947 --> 00:12:36,717
I feel so refreshed.

318
00:12:37,617 --> 00:12:39,446
I feel great. I feel refreshed.

319
00:12:39,447 --> 00:12:41,017
It looks like he's going out to exercise.

320
00:12:41,087 --> 00:12:42,356
- Is that a tennis outfit? - Right.

321
00:12:42,357 --> 00:12:44,157
- It looks like his tennis outfit. - Right.

322
00:12:45,357 --> 00:12:46,586
(Staring)

323
00:12:46,587 --> 00:12:48,757
My gosh, it's 7am on Sunday.

324
00:12:49,457 --> 00:12:50,996
I can't believe I'm up at this hour.

325
00:12:50,997 --> 00:12:52,396
- It's really early. - Let's go.

326
00:12:52,397 --> 00:12:54,297
Are you going to Sunday school? Why did you wake up so early?

327
00:12:57,397 --> 00:12:58,707
(Pulling)

328
00:12:58,767 --> 00:12:59,937
He'll play tennis.

329
00:13:01,377 --> 00:13:02,877
Wait. It's a badminton racket.

330
00:13:06,047 --> 00:13:09,176
(He goes out with a badminton racket around 7am.)

331
00:13:09,177 --> 00:13:10,347
At 7am?

332
00:13:11,217 --> 00:13:12,447
I'll play badminton.

333
00:13:13,617 --> 00:13:16,217
I always wanted to play badminton...

334
00:13:16,417 --> 00:13:17,517
when I played tennis.

335
00:13:17,927 --> 00:13:18,986
- But... - His weight loss is visible...

336
00:13:18,987 --> 00:13:20,026
with these old clips.

337
00:13:20,027 --> 00:13:21,057
(Right?)

338
00:13:21,327 --> 00:13:23,797
I met An Se Young once.

339
00:13:23,827 --> 00:13:26,526
After watching her play, I became fascinated by the sport.

340
00:13:26,527 --> 00:13:29,367
I always wanted to learn the techniques properly.

341
00:13:29,397 --> 00:13:32,266
Recently, thanks to this guy's influence,

342
00:13:32,267 --> 00:13:33,837
I started playing this sport.

343
00:13:33,867 --> 00:13:35,806
I went out to play with my senior athlete.

344
00:13:35,807 --> 00:13:37,236
- I signed up... - Who is it?

345
00:13:37,237 --> 00:13:38,446
to the same school.

346
00:13:38,447 --> 00:13:40,677
It's been 2 months. But I only attended 1 class...

347
00:13:40,907 --> 00:13:43,577
because I caught laryngitis right after the class.

348
00:13:44,887 --> 00:13:46,016
It's cold.

349
00:13:46,017 --> 00:13:48,217
(He was sad he couldn't play badminton due to laryngitis.)

350
00:13:48,857 --> 00:13:49,857
- Hey. - That's where...
- my senior athlete is. - It's cold.

351
00:13:50,858 --> 00:13:52,326
- Wait. You're not playing outside? - It's in the basement?

352
00:13:52,327 --> 00:13:53,457
It's an indoor court.

353
00:13:53,487 --> 00:13:54,896
Badminton is an indoor sport.

354
00:13:54,897 --> 00:13:56,357
- It can't be too windy. - Right.

355
00:13:56,427 --> 00:13:57,697
You can't play badminton outside.

356
00:13:58,867 --> 00:14:00,767
Gosh, you're here.

357
00:14:02,097 --> 00:14:03,236
Wait, his voice...

358
00:14:03,237 --> 00:14:04,706
(The mysterious senior was stretching.)

359
00:14:04,707 --> 00:14:06,337
- He seems familiar. - He's an everyday athlete.

360
00:14:06,507 --> 00:14:08,136
- Hold on. Gosh, what's going on? - Gosh.

361
00:14:08,137 --> 00:14:10,076
- He looks so handsome in this clip. - The athletic man.

362
00:14:10,077 --> 00:14:11,876
- Hold on. - He looks so handsome here.

363
00:14:11,877 --> 00:14:13,246
Wait. He looks like a national athlete.

364
00:14:13,247 --> 00:14:14,716
- He resembles the character... - Yes.

365
00:14:14,717 --> 00:14:15,877
- in "The Prince of Tennis." - Right.

366
00:14:15,977 --> 00:14:17,447
- He looks pretty good. - Yes.

367
00:14:17,887 --> 00:14:19,046
(Fancy footwork is a given.)

368
00:14:19,047 --> 00:14:20,517
- Gosh, he looks so professional. - Hey. My gosh. Oh, my.

369
00:14:21,617 --> 00:14:22,617
(Twitching)

370
00:14:22,618 --> 00:14:24,427
(He can deliver a strong smash shot too.)

371
00:14:24,787 --> 00:14:26,026
His name is Lee Ju Seung.

372
00:14:26,027 --> 00:14:27,156
Gosh, he looks cool.

373
00:14:27,157 --> 00:14:29,396
I heard from our instructor that he was quite good...

374
00:14:29,397 --> 00:14:30,926
only after playing for four months.

375
00:14:30,927 --> 00:14:31,927
Oh, my.

376
00:14:32,167 --> 00:14:34,166
(His shortening-distance technique trained his lower body.)

377
00:14:34,167 --> 00:14:35,197
It's been a while.

378
00:14:35,967 --> 00:14:37,136
His body moves swiftly.

379
00:14:37,137 --> 00:14:38,437
(All kinds of martial arts built a strong upper body.)

380
00:14:38,667 --> 00:14:40,536
He has the body of someone who exercises regularly.

381
00:14:40,537 --> 00:14:42,537
(He also trained his mind with zui quan.)

382
00:14:44,407 --> 00:14:45,747
What? That's you?

383
00:14:45,977 --> 00:14:47,506
- He's good. - Why is he so good?

384
00:14:47,507 --> 00:14:48,947
- Our instructor said he was good. - Gosh.

385
00:14:49,147 --> 00:14:51,076
Remember the day Ju Seung dropped you off?

386
00:14:51,077 --> 00:14:52,216
He played badminton before picking you up.

387
00:14:52,217 --> 00:14:53,917
- Right. That's where he was. - Right.

388
00:14:54,017 --> 00:14:55,056
It's close to my house.

389
00:14:55,057 --> 00:14:56,257
- That's why he went. - That's where he was.

390
00:14:57,217 --> 00:14:58,226
(Ju Seung drove Hyun Moo to the hospital...)

391
00:14:58,227 --> 00:14:59,286
(right after playing badminton.)

392
00:14:59,287 --> 00:15:00,856
- He played badminton before this. - What?

393
00:15:00,857 --> 00:15:02,427
- But... - He must sign up to the class.

394
00:15:02,557 --> 00:15:04,056
Then did you wake up at 6am too?

395
00:15:04,057 --> 00:15:05,567
I also woke up at 6am.

396
00:15:06,367 --> 00:15:07,896
Gosh, you're dressed in green too.

397
00:15:07,897 --> 00:15:09,496
My gosh. That was telepathy.

398
00:15:09,497 --> 00:15:10,836
(Two men dressed in deep green meet up to play badminton.)

399
00:15:10,837 --> 00:15:11,936
You look good today.

400
00:15:11,937 --> 00:15:13,236
But you don't look good.

401
00:15:13,237 --> 00:15:14,807
You're saying that when we just met?

402
00:15:15,507 --> 00:15:17,707
- Are you the instructor today? - I'm your instructor for the day.

403
00:15:18,047 --> 00:15:20,146
- I can teach a beginner like you. - No way.

404
00:15:20,147 --> 00:15:21,646
I can't believe this.

405
00:15:21,647 --> 00:15:23,477
- I can handle you. - He must be really good.

406
00:15:23,747 --> 00:15:25,616
- Why don't you grab the racket? - Yes.

407
00:15:25,617 --> 00:15:27,116
You're good enough to teach him?

408
00:15:27,117 --> 00:15:28,987
I learned the fundamentals.

409
00:15:29,057 --> 00:15:30,157
I took only one class.

410
00:15:31,457 --> 00:15:33,456
- You didn't learn the proper grip. - I did. What do you mean?

411
00:15:33,457 --> 00:15:35,797
You grab the racket as if you were shaking hands.

412
00:15:35,927 --> 00:15:37,457
You must be able to switch back and forth.

413
00:15:37,757 --> 00:15:38,796
I can do it.

414
00:15:38,797 --> 00:15:41,126
- Forehand and backhand. - Forehand and backhand.

415
00:15:41,127 --> 00:15:42,467
(He focuses on practicing the grip with Coach Ju Seung.)

416
00:15:42,867 --> 00:15:44,067
Let's warm up first.

417
00:15:44,667 --> 00:15:46,907
- Let's stretch our legs first. - Okay.

418
00:15:47,207 --> 00:15:48,406
You must always stretch your legs first.

419
00:15:48,407 --> 00:15:50,136
- Why do you sound so confident? - You're no match for me.

420
00:15:50,137 --> 00:15:51,707
- You're arrogant today. - No, listen.

421
00:15:51,877 --> 00:15:53,447
Shuttlecocks are my friends.

422
00:15:54,777 --> 00:15:56,246
He was bragging a lot.

423
00:15:56,247 --> 00:15:58,046
You seem livelier than the time...

424
00:15:58,047 --> 00:16:00,687
when you were shortening distance as Martial Artist Ju Seung.

425
00:16:00,847 --> 00:16:02,087
I guess you're really good.

426
00:16:02,757 --> 00:16:03,917
(Stretching)

427
00:16:04,117 --> 00:16:05,126
Look at you.

428
00:16:05,127 --> 00:16:06,987
- He was flexible at the temple too. - Right.

429
00:16:07,687 --> 00:16:08,757
Can you do this stretch?

430
00:16:11,297 --> 00:16:12,327
You can't do that?

431
00:16:12,627 --> 00:16:13,896
- I had never been able to do it. - Gosh.

432
00:16:13,897 --> 00:16:15,267
- I couldn't do it even as a kid. - My goodness.

433
00:16:15,967 --> 00:16:17,336
(Struggling)

434
00:16:17,337 --> 00:16:18,866
Do you have difficulty walking?

435
00:16:18,867 --> 00:16:20,006
(Joking)

436
00:16:20,007 --> 00:16:21,376
- Walking is tough for me. - What's wrong with you?

437
00:16:21,377 --> 00:16:22,907
My legs aren't flexible.

438
00:16:23,407 --> 00:16:25,277
Stretch your back too.

439
00:16:28,477 --> 00:16:29,847
He even circles his hips oddly.

440
00:16:30,447 --> 00:16:32,687
You remind me of a newborn elk.

441
00:16:33,287 --> 00:16:34,516
(Utterly ashamed)

442
00:16:34,517 --> 00:16:35,716
I'm just not flexible.

443
00:16:35,717 --> 00:16:37,616
- You're really inflexible. - I am.

444
00:16:37,617 --> 00:16:39,426
- You're a log. - Yes, I'm a log.

445
00:16:39,427 --> 00:16:40,926
- You can't circle your hips at all. - This isn't important...

446
00:16:40,927 --> 00:16:42,057
when playing tennis.

447
00:16:42,227 --> 00:16:44,357
- I can hit it right away. - Isn't this samba?

448
00:16:44,567 --> 00:16:46,227
- You're criticizing him a lot. - Yes.

449
00:16:47,297 --> 00:16:48,967
My gosh, you're so inflexible.

450
00:16:50,067 --> 00:16:51,767
His service will tell us everything.

451
00:16:55,007 --> 00:16:56,737
- My gosh. - That was swift.

452
00:16:56,807 --> 00:16:58,306
- My gosh. What? - Oh, my.

453
00:16:58,307 --> 00:16:59,477
- Ju Seung is good. - What was that?

454
00:17:00,707 --> 00:17:01,716
(Startled)

455
00:17:01,717 --> 00:17:03,377
(Flinging it down)

456
00:17:03,717 --> 00:17:04,846
- That's... - I wanted to make him laugh.

457
00:17:04,847 --> 00:17:05,946
- It was like... - Hey.

458
00:17:05,947 --> 00:17:07,886
swatting away a mosquito or a bee.

459
00:17:07,887 --> 00:17:09,257
- But you can't do that. - Gosh, this is making me mad.

460
00:17:09,817 --> 00:17:11,287
(He serves again.)

461
00:17:12,357 --> 00:17:14,997
(Coach Ju Seung takes care of it with ease.)

462
00:17:15,097 --> 00:17:16,296
(Falling)

463
00:17:16,297 --> 00:17:17,727
What do I do when it's too low?

464
00:17:18,127 --> 00:17:19,496
Then you must lower your body like this.

465
00:17:19,497 --> 00:17:20,767
- Lower my body? - I see.

466
00:17:20,867 --> 00:17:22,667
Or you must change to a backhand grip and hit it.

467
00:17:24,037 --> 00:17:25,267
As for Hyun Moo,

468
00:17:25,837 --> 00:17:27,937
the color of his face has been off.

469
00:17:27,977 --> 00:17:30,436
He seemed to be losing energy lately.

470
00:17:30,437 --> 00:17:31,806
His face was sagging too.

471
00:17:31,807 --> 00:17:33,107
He doesn't have energy these days.

472
00:17:33,277 --> 00:17:35,077
I thought that learning badminton...

473
00:17:35,247 --> 00:17:38,146
would hopefully make his body flexible.

474
00:17:38,147 --> 00:17:39,986
He must train a lot to improve.

475
00:17:39,987 --> 00:17:43,017
So I kept trying to push him to hit the shuttlecock.

476
00:17:44,287 --> 00:17:46,026
- He sounds like a coach. - He's talking like a coach.

477
00:17:46,027 --> 00:17:47,757
- Like a coach. - Like a coach for a national team.

478
00:17:47,887 --> 00:17:49,226
- He thinks Hyun Moo is... - Yes.

479
00:17:49,227 --> 00:17:50,497
- three levels beneath him. - Right.

480
00:17:51,497 --> 00:17:53,667
He's talking about Hyun Moo like Hyun Moo is his junior.

481
00:17:53,927 --> 00:17:56,397
Hey, let's make a wager.

482
00:17:56,797 --> 00:17:58,267
- Let's play for ten points. - What?

483
00:17:58,567 --> 00:17:59,937
- A wager? - The loser buys lunch.

484
00:18:00,037 --> 00:18:01,806
The loser buys lunch? Okay.

485
00:18:01,807 --> 00:18:03,437
Okay. I got it. Nice.

486
00:18:04,877 --> 00:18:06,947
(The game to score 10 points begins.)

487
00:18:08,217 --> 00:18:10,217
I can manage a basic serve. Yes.

488
00:18:12,487 --> 00:18:13,587
That's a nice sound.

489
00:18:14,217 --> 00:18:16,257
(They trade shots with utter intensity.)

490
00:18:18,127 --> 00:18:19,526
(It lands inside the court.)

491
00:18:19,527 --> 00:18:20,826
- Darn it. - It's 1 to 0.

492
00:18:20,827 --> 00:18:21,857
- My gosh, yes. - Oh, my.

493
00:18:21,997 --> 00:18:23,157
Ju Seung is good.

494
00:18:23,927 --> 00:18:24,966
Nice.

495
00:18:24,967 --> 00:18:26,296
(Did you see that, Hyun Moo?)

496
00:18:26,297 --> 00:18:27,297
I got a point.

497
00:18:27,298 --> 00:18:29,267
- Give me the shuttlecock. - That was a nasty shot.

498
00:18:31,197 --> 00:18:32,707
(Ju Seung: 1, Hyun Moo: 0)

499
00:18:32,807 --> 00:18:37,507
You must know how to disguise shots whether they're long or short.

500
00:18:38,677 --> 00:18:39,746
(Zooming by)

501
00:18:39,747 --> 00:18:40,876
That was sneaky.

502
00:18:40,877 --> 00:18:42,417
- There. - Don't you think that was sneaky?

503
00:18:42,817 --> 00:18:43,946
- Gosh. - Right.

504
00:18:43,947 --> 00:18:45,386
- The mind game is important. - You're good.

505
00:18:45,387 --> 00:18:46,917
It's important to figure out if it will be a long or short shot.

506
00:18:47,247 --> 00:18:49,856
Beginners can't hit back a long shot.

507
00:18:49,857 --> 00:18:50,957
We can't.

508
00:18:51,457 --> 00:18:53,157
(It's Ju Seung's service again.)

509
00:18:54,387 --> 00:18:56,657
(Moomoo loses another point.)

510
00:18:57,597 --> 00:18:59,297
You're trying to score points with your service.

511
00:18:59,367 --> 00:19:00,997
We can go on since you can't hit back my serve.

512
00:19:01,097 --> 00:19:02,797
