769
00:27:03,681 --> 00:27:05,681
- I didn't see that coming. - Gosh.

770
00:27:06,911 --> 00:27:08,010
I'll end it.

771
00:27:08,011 --> 00:27:09,681
(I'll end this now.)

772
00:27:10,381 --> 00:27:13,551
(Looking determined)

773
00:27:14,091 --> 00:27:16,120
(It goes back and forth in a sharp rally.)

774
00:27:16,121 --> 00:27:17,790
- Nice. - That's good.

775
00:27:17,791 --> 00:27:18,831
Nice.

776
00:27:19,291 --> 00:27:21,161
- Nice. - Keep playing to the end.

777
00:27:21,231 --> 00:27:22,461
- I hit it back. - He hit it up.

778
00:27:22,561 --> 00:27:24,230
- He hit it up. - That's instant agility.

779
00:27:24,231 --> 00:27:25,401
- That's An Se Young. - My gosh.

780
00:27:25,531 --> 00:27:26,630
- That's amazing. - I'm Moo Se Young.

781
00:27:26,631 --> 00:27:27,931
- Moo Se Young. - Nice.

782
00:27:28,331 --> 00:27:30,141
- Nice. - It's the An Se Young move.

783
00:27:30,771 --> 00:27:31,771
Nice.

784
00:27:31,772 --> 00:27:32,840
- You couldn't hit it back? - It's the An Se Young move.

785
00:27:32,841 --> 00:27:35,010
- How could he hit it back? - The An Se Young move. It's over.

786
00:27:35,011 --> 00:27:36,011
(Hyun Moo wins.)

787
00:27:36,441 --> 00:27:37,480
(After winning the match,)

788
00:27:37,481 --> 00:27:38,511
(An Se Young opened up her arms to celebrate.)

789
00:27:38,881 --> 00:27:40,481
- Shuttlecock Prince Moo Se Young. - The An Se Young move. It's over.

790
00:27:41,411 --> 00:27:43,120
- You lost in the end? - You lost?

791
00:27:43,121 --> 00:27:44,151
He did.

792
00:27:44,581 --> 00:27:45,621
It's over.

793
00:27:46,151 --> 00:27:47,321
It was a good game.

794
00:27:48,491 --> 00:27:50,461
By the way, my last shot was pretty cool, right?

795
00:27:51,061 --> 00:27:52,831
I'll tell everyone that I won.

796
00:27:54,731 --> 00:27:55,861
Are you tired?

797
00:27:57,801 --> 00:27:59,331
I heard you were in good shape.

798
00:27:59,571 --> 00:28:01,801
You didn't move around.

799
00:28:02,241 --> 00:28:03,301
But I did.

800
00:28:03,441 --> 00:28:04,771
But I still won.

801
00:28:05,341 --> 00:28:06,770
Imagine what would happen if I moved around.

802
00:28:06,771 --> 00:28:07,840
(Feeling miserable)

803
00:28:07,841 --> 00:28:08,981
You'd be in big trouble.

804
00:28:09,681 --> 00:28:10,841
That was a good game.

805
00:28:13,581 --> 00:28:14,610
I heard you could play for hours.

806
00:28:14,611 --> 00:28:15,981
Why are you so weak?

807
00:28:16,221 --> 00:28:17,520
It's not that I'm weak.

808
00:28:17,521 --> 00:28:19,951
You drained my energy because you kept insisting it was in.

809
00:28:21,151 --> 00:28:22,991
You said that even before it hit the floor.

810
00:28:23,421 --> 00:28:24,660
To be fair,

811
00:28:24,661 --> 00:28:25,890
- the victory should go to him. - Yes.

812
00:28:25,891 --> 00:28:27,330
Actually, I was shocked...

813
00:28:27,331 --> 00:28:28,731
- after playing that game. - Yes.

814
00:28:28,831 --> 00:28:31,231
I made a promise to my instructor that I'd train at least once a week.

815
00:28:31,561 --> 00:28:33,800
- When I'm somewhat ready, - You'll train?

816
00:28:33,801 --> 00:28:35,740
- I'll challenge you formally. - Another one?

817
00:28:35,741 --> 00:28:37,070
- Great. - Really?

818
00:28:37,071 --> 00:28:38,200
- I mean it. - "I forgot."

819
00:28:38,201 --> 00:28:39,440
You should play doubles at a competition.

820
00:28:39,441 --> 00:28:40,970
I want us to play doubles together.

821
00:28:40,971 --> 00:28:42,510
- You want to compete? - Yes.

822
00:28:42,511 --> 00:28:43,710
- There's one for beginners. - Yes.

823
00:28:43,711 --> 00:28:45,450
It will be just beginners at the competition.

824
00:28:45,451 --> 00:28:47,481
- There's one for beginners. Yes. - Yes. For beginners.

825
00:28:47,611 --> 00:28:48,921
Hey, we played for two hours.

826
00:28:49,621 --> 00:28:50,950
- It was a good workout. - You played hard.

827
00:28:50,951 --> 00:28:52,321
Badminton can help you lose weight.

828
00:28:53,121 --> 00:28:56,061
I've been training here for four months now.

829
00:28:58,291 --> 00:28:59,490
This was the most draining session.

830
00:28:59,491 --> 00:29:00,860
You didn't go over what would be considered in.

831
00:29:00,861 --> 00:29:01,861
- It must cross this line. - I forgot.

832
00:29:01,862 --> 00:29:03,931
I keep hearing his voice saying, "It's in."

833
00:29:04,031 --> 00:29:05,671
You're so out of it.

834
00:29:06,871 --> 00:29:09,741
Hey. I know that I barely moved around.

835
00:29:10,171 --> 00:29:11,701
But since it's fun, it's a good workout.

836
00:29:11,801 --> 00:29:13,371
(I see.)

837
00:29:13,871 --> 00:29:16,811
After playing badminton, I saw the need to keep at it.

838
00:29:17,581 --> 00:29:19,480
It makes you lose fat fast.

839
00:29:19,481 --> 00:29:20,550
- That's right. - This?

840
00:29:20,551 --> 00:29:22,421
You're sweating so much after playing with me.

841
00:29:23,021 --> 00:29:25,151
- Look at the sweat on your neck. - He's flushing now.

842
00:29:25,251 --> 00:29:26,791
It's an intense cardio workout.

843
00:29:27,021 --> 00:29:28,420
- Of course. - It's really intense.

844
00:29:28,421 --> 00:29:29,961
- It's an intense cardio workout. - It must be.

845
00:29:30,361 --> 00:29:33,261
We must have a referee next time we play together.

846
00:29:33,491 --> 00:29:34,991
You keep forgetting the rules.

847
00:29:35,501 --> 00:29:36,831
(Embarrassed)

848
00:29:37,331 --> 00:29:38,500
Did you drink something?

849
00:29:38,501 --> 00:29:39,701
I did.

850
00:29:40,801 --> 00:29:42,040
(Gulping down)

851
00:29:42,041 --> 00:29:43,270
It must be refreshing after working out.

852
00:29:43,271 --> 00:29:44,471
It's good to drink it.

853
00:29:44,841 --> 00:29:46,611
- Gosh, it's so refreshing. - It was really refreshing.

854
00:29:46,841 --> 00:29:48,311
It's making up for the sweat I lost.

855
00:29:50,241 --> 00:29:51,641
I used to play badminton a lot.

856
00:29:52,551 --> 00:29:55,251
It's Sunday, and it's not even 9am yet.

857
00:29:55,451 --> 00:29:57,151
Exactly. Why did you call me so early in the morning?

858
00:29:57,421 --> 00:30:00,191
I wanted to make the day long.

859
00:30:00,591 --> 00:30:02,121
- At 9am? - Yes. Let's go eat.

860
00:30:02,661 --> 00:30:04,021
- You want to eat when it's 9am? - Yes.

861
00:30:04,461 --> 00:30:05,490
It's been a while for me too.

862
00:30:05,491 --> 00:30:07,131
- It's breakfast for you. - Of course.

863
00:30:07,631 --> 00:30:09,200
It wasn't even brunch. It was breakfast.

864
00:30:09,201 --> 00:30:10,701
- Yes, it's breakfast. - I bet no place is open.

865
00:30:11,301 --> 00:30:12,371
Where should we eat?

866
00:30:14,101 --> 00:30:15,701
There's udon, soba, and...

867
00:30:16,671 --> 00:30:17,871
How about hand-cut kalguksu?

868
00:30:18,441 --> 00:30:19,541
That's a good place.

869
00:30:19,671 --> 00:30:21,141
It's where I go often.

870
00:30:21,441 --> 00:30:23,311
- Why didn't you tell me? - I've been going there since young.

871
00:30:23,541 --> 00:30:25,350
- But at this hour... - You've been going there...

872
00:30:25,351 --> 00:30:26,480
since young, but why did I look up that place?

873
00:30:26,481 --> 00:30:27,651
I mean...

874
00:30:27,781 --> 00:30:29,181
Because it opens at 11:30am.

875
00:30:29,621 --> 00:30:31,650
- Let's eat there later. - Sure.

876
00:30:31,651 --> 00:30:33,751
Are you willing to work out more?

877
00:30:34,091 --> 00:30:35,290
- Work out? - Yes.

878
00:30:35,291 --> 00:30:37,361
I'm not tired yet, so...

879
00:30:38,321 --> 00:30:40,161
Then let's not drive to the restaurant.

880
00:30:41,461 --> 00:30:42,861
Let's get there by slow jogging.

881
00:30:43,001 --> 00:30:44,830
- What is that? - What is slow jogging?

882
00:30:44,831 --> 00:30:46,030
I hear that's trending these days.

883
00:30:46,031 --> 00:30:48,071
So many people recommended it to me.

884
00:30:48,531 --> 00:30:49,871
- Slow jogging? - Yes.

885
00:30:51,571 --> 00:30:54,871
More people have been recommending slow jogging than running to me.

886
00:30:55,171 --> 00:30:56,380
I heard it was really good.

887
00:30:56,381 --> 00:30:58,141
- I've never heard of slow jogging. - I thought, "Let's go jogging."

888
00:30:58,281 --> 00:31:00,811
I've never heard of such things, but he always says they're trending.

889
00:31:01,081 --> 00:31:02,121
You don't know what it is?

890
00:31:02,681 --> 00:31:03,920
It's not fast walking?

891
00:31:03,921 --> 00:31:05,121
It's different from race walking?

892
00:31:05,221 --> 00:31:07,451
It's jogging slowly, strictly speaking.

893
00:31:07,851 --> 00:31:09,461
- That is running. - That's...

894
00:31:09,661 --> 00:31:11,420
When you run, you control your pace...

895
00:31:11,421 --> 00:31:12,730
- by going slow and then fast. - You control your pace as you run.

896
00:31:12,731 --> 00:31:13,890
I'm not talking about going that slow.

897
00:31:13,891 --> 00:31:15,291
- Oh, is that so? - See how slow I jog.

898
00:31:15,561 --> 00:31:17,201
- Then that's walking. - That's walking.

899
00:31:17,561 --> 00:31:18,661
No, it's not.

900
00:31:19,431 --> 00:31:20,871
- What do you mean? - You'll realize it when you see it.

901
00:31:21,031 --> 00:31:23,600
I could tolerate Yin-Yang Water.

902
00:31:23,601 --> 00:31:25,540
- Right. That was too much. - Stop making things up anymore.

903
00:31:25,541 --> 00:31:26,670
It's something in between...

904
00:31:26,671 --> 00:31:27,770
- walking and running. - I mean...

905
00:31:27,771 --> 00:31:30,240
- Really? - Hashtag, slow jogging. Look it up.

906
00:31:30,241 --> 00:31:31,880
I've never seen such hashtags.

907
00:31:31,881 --> 00:31:34,051
- I've never seen it either. - Just take a look.

908
00:31:34,251 --> 00:31:37,321
I saw the video of slow jogging, and it didn't look that hard.

909
00:31:38,221 --> 00:31:40,251
- Look at that. - That's running.

910
00:31:40,551 --> 00:31:42,221
I guess it's a new type.

911
00:31:42,591 --> 00:31:44,821
Seongsu-dong isn't that far from Gangnam.

912
00:31:45,061 --> 00:31:47,161
It's around 3km to 4km.

913
00:31:47,661 --> 00:31:50,400
Running a few kilometers itself...

914
00:31:50,401 --> 00:31:51,561
was a challenge for me.

915
00:31:51,801 --> 00:31:52,970
Let's run to Seongsu-dong, then.

916
00:31:52,971 --> 00:31:54,671
- Slow jogging? - Yes, slow jogging.

917
00:31:54,871 --> 00:31:56,041
It's trending these days.

918
00:31:56,201 --> 00:31:57,971
It's my 1st time hearing it in the 42 years of my life.

919
00:31:58,101 --> 00:31:59,511
So you don't look up hashtags.

920
00:31:59,771 --> 00:32:02,181
- Do you only do things that trend? - Yes. I don't do it if it's old.

921
00:32:05,311 --> 00:32:06,711
- Is this how you do it? - Go like this.

922
00:32:07,411 --> 00:32:09,081
Make sure the ball of your foot touches the ground first.

923
00:32:09,781 --> 00:32:11,281
This is running.

924
00:32:11,851 --> 00:32:13,020
What happens if you run?

925
00:32:13,021 --> 00:32:15,150
It impacts your knees.

926
00:32:15,151 --> 00:32:16,721
But if you let the ball of your foot touch the ground first,

927
00:32:16,921 --> 00:32:18,790
- your joints are less strained. - Oh, the ball of your foot?

928
00:32:18,791 --> 00:32:20,460
You're right. The ball of your foot...

929
00:32:20,461 --> 00:32:22,561
- absorbs the shock. - Right?

930
00:32:23,601 --> 00:32:25,331
And you keep moving your body too.

931
00:32:26,271 --> 00:32:28,130
- Your whole body. - If you feel like you can run fast,

932
00:32:28,131 --> 00:32:29,200
- can you? - No, you'll be told off...

933
00:32:29,201 --> 00:32:30,271
because it strains your joints.

934
00:32:30,841 --> 00:32:32,041
This is what they call slow jogging.

935
00:32:32,471 --> 00:32:34,741
- Did you learn it? - No, I watched a video about it.

936
00:32:36,541 --> 00:32:38,341
People kept saying that it's trending these days.

937
00:32:39,281 --> 00:32:40,950
It must raise my heart rate a bit.

938
00:32:40,951 --> 00:32:42,051
Of course.

939
00:32:42,981 --> 00:32:44,251
Did you quit warping?

940
00:32:44,821 --> 00:32:46,621
I haven't been doing it because of my knees.

941
00:32:47,121 --> 00:32:48,621
We could apply warping in slow jogging.

942
00:32:50,461 --> 00:32:51,591
Like this.

943
00:32:52,461 --> 00:32:53,631
This is much harder, right?

944
00:32:54,731 --> 00:32:56,631
I think warping is slower than slow jogging.

945
00:32:57,231 --> 00:32:59,571
I bet if we use warping,

946
00:32:59,901 --> 00:33:01,171
we'll get there in 15 minutes.

947
00:33:01,931 --> 00:33:03,171
That'd be as fast as a car.

948
00:33:03,941 --> 00:33:05,171
(Giggling)

949
00:33:05,911 --> 00:33:07,170
Keep your arms at a 90-degree angle.

950
00:33:07,171 --> 00:33:08,540
(A miracle morning on an empty street to strengthen your immunity)

951
00:33:08,541 --> 00:33:09,711
You need to use your whole body.

952
00:33:11,111 --> 00:33:12,180
If there's a red light,

953
00:33:12,181 --> 00:33:13,711
- should we jog in place? - We should.

954
00:33:13,881 --> 00:33:15,311
If you stop, everything will be in vain.

955
00:33:15,921 --> 00:33:17,280
You need to keep jogging. You shouldn't stop.

956
00:33:17,281 --> 00:33:19,820
- You can't stop. Keep going. - What if you need to pee?

957
00:33:19,821 --> 00:33:22,220
- You should pee as you jog. - Pee as you jog?

958
00:33:22,221 --> 00:33:23,960
(You should pee as you jog.)

959
00:33:23,961 --> 00:33:26,161
- You need to dry it as you jog. - That's slow jogging?

960
00:33:26,861 --> 00:33:28,830
You must be jogging even in the restroom.

961
00:33:28,831 --> 00:33:30,261
- Really? Even in the restroom? - Yes.

962
00:33:30,361 --> 00:33:32,671
You'll be told off by the cleaning people.

963
00:33:32,771 --> 00:33:34,170
Then do you have to keep jogging as you're being told off?

964
00:33:34,171 --> 00:33:36,101
You should with your hands behind your back.

965
00:33:37,701 --> 00:33:39,411
"I'm sorry. It's my fault."

966
00:33:39,911 --> 00:33:41,110
- "It's splattering all over." - "Sorry."

967
00:33:41,111 --> 00:33:42,441
"I'll wipe that later."

968
00:33:43,111 --> 00:33:44,611
It is clearly different from running.

969
00:33:45,081 --> 00:33:46,780
- Now I finally get it. - It doesn't give you time to rest.

970
00:33:46,781 --> 00:33:48,011
It is really different.

971
00:33:48,751 --> 00:33:50,750
(They've been running in place for a while, waiting for the green light.)

972
00:33:50,751 --> 00:33:53,321
Ju Seung is doing his best to follow him.

973
00:33:53,951 --> 00:33:55,021
All right.

974
00:33:55,761 --> 00:33:57,390
I can't believe we're running on this street.

975
00:33:57,391 --> 00:33:58,521
I always drive past here.

976
00:33:58,791 --> 00:34:00,760
- It must be tiring, though. - It is.

977
00:34:00,761 --> 00:34:01,860
It makes you sweat a lot.

978
00:34:01,861 --> 00:34:04,531
It is definitely less straining on your joints.

979
00:34:05,461 --> 00:34:06,870
Are your joints in bad shape now?

980
00:34:06,871 --> 00:34:08,201
They're in good shape.

981
00:34:08,901 --> 00:34:11,240
Running on asphalt is really bad for your joints.

982
00:34:11,241 --> 00:34:12,511
(As they take care of their joint health...)

983
00:34:13,211 --> 00:34:14,370
It's Yeongdong Bridge.

984
00:34:14,371 --> 00:34:15,811
(They're on Yeongdong Bridge in no time.)

985
00:34:15,911 --> 00:34:17,681
Do you know a song called "Yeongdong Bridge in the Rain?"

986
00:34:18,781 --> 00:34:19,881
No.

987
00:34:20,611 --> 00:34:24,151
(On Yeongdong Bridge on a rainy night)

988
00:34:25,281 --> 00:34:27,950
(Walking there by myself)

989
00:34:27,951 --> 00:34:29,421
- You don't know the song? - You said you were TSM.

990
00:34:30,091 --> 00:34:33,461
("Yeongdong Bridge in the Rain" by Joo Hyun Mi)

991
00:34:34,291 --> 00:34:35,700
Jennie could do a remake of the song.

992
00:34:35,701 --> 00:34:37,501
Trot Sensitive Man, not Trend Sensitive Man.

993
00:34:37,761 --> 00:34:38,971
Isn't that a song from my grandma's time?

994
00:34:40,131 --> 00:34:41,771
- I think I've heard of it. - You're acting like you're an MZ.

995
00:34:43,041 --> 00:34:44,601
You guys look like healthy father and son.

996
00:34:45,871 --> 00:34:46,871
Right. They look like...
- father and son. - Exactly.

997
00:34:48,071 --> 00:34:49,941
It's good to see you two running together.

998
00:34:50,081 --> 00:34:53,211
(Running on Yeongdong Bridge with the dad's youth)

999
00:34:53,611 --> 00:34:55,451
I watched the merits of slow jogging...

1000
00:34:56,421 --> 00:34:57,721
on "Mysteries of the Human Body."

1001
00:34:58,621 --> 00:35:01,121
The case subjects weren't much different from me.

1002
00:35:01,551 --> 00:35:03,361
As in their lifestyles or their body conditions.

1003
00:35:04,461 --> 00:35:06,160
("Gwangju's Seo-gu Opens the Era of Living Healthy with Slow Jogging")

1004
00:35:06,161 --> 00:35:07,861
(Stop worrying about your joints!)

1005
00:35:08,861 --> 00:35:10,700
(People of all generations enjoy slow jogging.)

1006
00:35:10,701 --> 00:35:12,371
Maybe it was developed for the elderly.

1007
00:35:13,301 --> 00:35:14,400
A dad's challenge.

1008
00:35:14,401 --> 00:35:15,701
A dad's challenge?

1009
00:35:16,201 --> 00:35:17,371
Hang in there, Dad.

1010
00:35:18,841 --> 00:35:21,411
- You really kept going. - We never stopped.

1011
00:35:21,511 --> 00:35:22,941
I only said that because it made sense.

1012
00:35:25,751 --> 00:35:27,480
- Look at Ju Seung. - He stopped.

1013
00:35:27,481 --> 00:35:29,581
- That's what he did. - He stopped.

1014
00:35:30,181 --> 00:35:31,551
- We need to keep jogging. - We need to press this.

1015
00:35:32,391 --> 00:35:33,991
Don't use that as an excuse.

1016
00:35:35,021 --> 00:35:36,121
What time is it?

1017
00:35:37,421 --> 00:35:39,060
We need to run in place while waiting for the green light.

1018
00:35:39,061 --> 00:35:40,791
- Your arms. There you go. - He's getting tired.

1019
00:35:40,991 --> 00:35:43,531
